 "summary": "The lambda calculus restricted by simple (arrow) types, introduced by Church in 1940 as the simple theory of types; it is strongly normalising (hence not Turing-complete), corresponds to intuitionistic propositional logic via Curry-Howard, and is the base case of nearly every typed functional language and type-soundness proof.",
 "status": "theoretical",
