  "0": "Theoretical calculus: level 0 lists mechanised definitions and soundness/normalisation proofs (Software Foundations/Coq, PLFA/Agda, Isabelle, Metalib) and the TAPL reference type checkers.",
  "1": "Church's 1940 JSL paper defines the simple theory of types; Curry (for the Curry-style variant), Tait (1967, normalisation) and Howard (1969/1980, formulae-as-types) are the other primary sources."
